## What Problem This Solves

Fixes an issue where the dependency pin guard could hang indefinitely when Git stopped returning tracked package manifests or index-backed package JSON.

## Why This Change Was Made

The dependency pin checker now applies a fixed one-minute timeout to its `git ls-files` and `git show :...` subprocesses and reports the stalled Git command. Focused tests inject a shorter timeout through the existing module boundary without adding an operator-facing environment setting.

## User Impact

Developers and CI jobs get a clear dependency-pin failure instead of a stuck validation step.

## Evidence

- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/check-dependency-pins.test.ts` — 5 tests passed, including the portable stalled-Git fixture.
- Production-module proof exercises `collectDependencyPinViolations` with both a completing and stalled Git boundary:

```text
$ node proof-dependency-pins-timeout.mjs
valid: completed=true violations=0
stalled: dependency pin guard: git ls-files -z -- *package.json timed out after 500ms.
```

<details>
<summary>proof-dependency-pins-timeout.mjs</summary>

```js
import fs from "node:fs/promises";
import os from "node:os";
import path from "node:path";
import { collectDependencyPinViolations } from "./scripts/check-dependency-pins.mjs";

const tempRoot = await fs.mkdtemp(path.join(os.tmpdir(), "openclaw-dependency-pins-proof-"));
const binDir = path.join(tempRoot, "bin");
await fs.mkdir(binDir);
const originalPath = process.env.PATH;

async function writeGitFixture(body) {
  if (process.platform === "win32") {
    const fixturePath = path.join(binDir, "git-fixture.mjs");
    await fs.writeFile(fixturePath, body);
    await fs.writeFile(path.join(binDir, "git.cmd"), `@echo off\r\n"${process.execPath}" "${fixturePath}" %*\r\n`);
    return;
  }
  await fs.writeFile(path.join(binDir, "git"), `#!${process.execPath}\n${body}`, { mode: 0o755 });
}

try {
  process.env.PATH = binDir;
  await writeGitFixture("process.exit(0);\n");
  const valid = collectDependencyPinViolations(tempRoot, { gitTimeoutMs: 500 });
  console.log(`valid: completed=true violations=${valid.length}`);

  await writeGitFixture('if (process.argv[2] === "ls-files") { setTimeout(() => {}, 10_000); }\nelse { process.exit(0); }\n');
  try {
    collectDependencyPinViolations(tempRoot, { gitTimeoutMs: 500 });
  } catch (error) {
    console.log(`stalled: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`);
  }
} finally {
  process.env.PATH = originalPath;
  await fs.rm(tempRoot, { recursive: true, force: true });
}
```

</details>

